# Agent Discipline Core (monitor workspace)

**Why this file exists:** The monitor workspace has **30+** domain rules. Loading all of them every turn causes **attention collapse**—agents skip steps you marked important. This file is the **always-on control plane**. Domain rules are **binding when triggered**; you must **Read** them (tool), not guess.

**Cursor Settings User Rules count equally** with workspace rules. If they conflict on close discipline, follow the **stricter** requirement.

## Always-on companions (read every session)

| Rule | Law |
|------|-----|
| **`plan-completion-gate.mdc`** | No "done" without **Final code review (senior engineer pass)** + **Post-implementation review** (all non-trivial code changes) |
| **`every-error-regression-test.mdc`** | Every fix for a failure needs a regression test before close |
| **`monitor-workspace-contract.mdc`** | Monitor-only edits under `HPCPerfStats/monitor/`; consumer contract via `listend.py` |
| **`python-venv-enforcement.mdc`** | Single `<workspace_root>/.venv/bin/python`; edit rules in `HPCPerfStats/monitor/cursor-rules/` |
| **`workspace-single-cursor-directory.mdc`** | Exactly one `<workspace_root>/.cursor/`; never `HPCPerfStats/.cursor/` or other nested `.cursor/` |
| **`out-of-monitor-hpcperfstats-rules.mdc`** | When user authorizes non-monitor edits, load `hpcperfstats/cursor-rules/` for that work |

## Pre-close checklist (verify before final message)

Answer **YES** or **N/A (one-line reason)** for each row. If any row is **NO**, keep working.

| # | Check |
|---|--------|
| 1 | **Senior code review** section written (`## Final code review (senior engineer pass)`) |
| 2 | **Post-implementation review** written (Why it works, ≥3 edge cases, convention check) |
| 3 | **Regression test** added/updated for every failure/bug fixed (`every-error-regression-test.mdc`) |
| 4 | **Relevant tests executed** (`make check`, static bundle, cross-compile when applicable); pass/fail reported; log under `test_runs/` if run |
| 5 | **Triggered domain rules** below were **Read** (Read tool on the `.mdc` path) before editing — list them under **`## Agent rule dispatch`** at close; hook verifies Read calls for listed domain rules |
| 6 | **Dual verify** run when substantive monitor C changed (`monitor-dual-verify-cross-and-static.mdc`) |
| 7 | **Plan YAML** todos synced if implementing a plan (`plan-completion-gate.mdc`) |
| 8 | **New/re-triggered domain rules** dual-registered in **both** this file (task router) and `cursor-hooks/hook_task_router.py` (`MONITOR_ROUTER_ENTRIES`) — verify in **Final code review** when the diff touches `cursor-rules/*.mdc` |

User may reply **`Close gate incomplete`** — redo the full close sequence without argument.

